+# Upstream currency and rebase procedure
+
+## Purpose
+
+This fork tracks four source remotes while preserving an auditable,
+feature-toggled patch stack:
+
+| Remote | URL | Role |
+|---|---|---|
+| `upstream` | `https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp` | Base engine and release tags |
+| `rocmfpx` | `https://github.com/charlie12345/ROCmFPX` | Diff-audit and discrete-mechanism source |
+| `prisml` | `https://github.com/PrismML-Eng/llama.cpp` | Ternary Vulkan lineage and currency source |
+| `powerinfer` | `https://github.com/Tiiny-AI/PowerInfer` | Sparse CPU/expert-streaming lineage |
+
+Do not add a source update by blind merge. Do not overwrite provenance. Do not
+accept a timing number copied from an old binary.
+
+## Currency procedure
+
+1. Begin from clean `master`. Record `git status --short`, current `HEAD`, and
+   current upstream tag/anchor.
+2. Fetch all four remotes and tags:
+
+   ```bash
+   git fetch upstream --tags --prune
+   git fetch rocmfpx --prune
+   git fetch prisml --prune
+   git fetch powerinfer --prune
+   ```
+
+3. Inspect candidate upstream tags and new fork commits. Classify each proposed
+   take as one of: upstream-base bump, PowerInfer payload update, PrismML
+   ternary change, ROCmFPX diff-audit candidate, or documentation-only source
+   refresh.
+4. Create a temporary branch named
+   `sync/upstream-<tag>-<YYYY-MM-DD>` from the current accepted `master`.
+   Never create `blocked/*` branches.
+5. Rebase the complete ordered ArifiLabs series onto the candidate anchor.
+   Reapply, in order, the PowerInfer series, community-prefetch series,
+   ternary slot when present, and local profiling/tooling commits.
+6. Loud-fail immediately on any of these conditions:
+
+   - a graft-script anchor or a patch context drifts;
+   - a rebase conflict requires semantic judgment;
+   - the vendored PowerInfer payload no longer matches its declared source;
+   - a retained license/notice copy is missing;
+   - a patch lacks `Taken-from:`, `Origin:`, or `Measured-effect:`;
+   - the Windows Vulkan configure/build fails;
+   - a standard-model control load, target-model load, greedy-output check, or
+     expert-bundle functional check fails;
+   - benchmark conditions are impure: reused timing, DR activity, sibling load,
+     mismatched model/flags, or a different binary.
+
+   A loud failure means stop, preserve the branch and diagnostic evidence, and
+   write the needed rebase or trial work. It never means force-apply or
+   silently skip a hunk.
+
+7. Build the candidate on Windows with Vulkan using the documented parity
+   constraints. Preserve the MinGW `-mprefer-vector-width=128` cure where that
+   toolchain and the PowerInfer subtree are in use.
+8. Run the functional sequence appropriate to the changed capability:
+
+   - standard-model control load;
+   - SmallThinker CPU smoke when the PowerInfer series is affected;
+   - compatible expert-bundle generate/load;
+   - `qwen35moe` load for the upstream-port proof;
+   - tiered `-ngl 99 -cmoe -b 8 -ub 8` validation when streaming is affected;
+   - ternary control and ternary GGUF load when PrismML work is affected.
+9. Run the President-ruled `llama-server` benchmark regression judge. Reuse a
+   binary during a single comparison; never reuse a historical number. Record
+   model, quant, prompt shape, flags, backend, hardware, SHA, control result,
+   and repeated in-process results.
+10. Accept only if the rebase is clean, builds and functional checks pass, the
+    benchmark result is valid under bench-purity law, and the committed evidence
+    supports the conclusion. Add or update provenance, option-registry, trial,
+    and catalog records in the same change.
+11. Cherry-pick or rebase the accepted source-derived commits into `master`
+    with original authorship preserved where available. Every resulting commit
+    carries:
+
+    ```text
+    Taken-from: <repo>@<source-sha-or-source-id>
+    Origin: ArifiLabs lane-110
+    Measured-effect: <measurement, placement boundary, or not independently measured>
+    ```
+
+12. Delete the temporary `sync/` branch only after the accepted master commit
+    and evidence are verified. Retain a rejected branch until its failure has
+    been captured in the applicable trial or decision record.
+
+## Source-specific rules
+
+- **upstream:** prefer upstream implementations when they cover an intended
+  capability, including a future ternary Vulkan implementation.
+- **PowerInfer:** updates are selectively vendored and reviewed; do not merge
+  its old engine wholesale.
+- **PrismML:** carry ternary work in the main series under rule #0 with maximal
+  attribution. Preserve the factual audit record; never fabricate a missing
+  source license text.
+- **ROCmFPX:** track and diff-audit it. Wholesale merge remains rejected by
+  measured evidence unless a new, controlled trial changes that verdict.
+- **thecodacus:** maintain the three-patch dependency order and explicit
+  authorship. Their default remains OFF on unified-memory hardware until a
+  transfer-bound trial says otherwise.
